GPL does not prevent sale of software, as Titus pointed out you do need to provide the code if you do. There are also plenty of GPL compatible licenses you could write a package under.

Data is not covered under the GPL, so yes you can continue to charge for access to the data the packages uses.

Your employer should pay a lawyer to work out the issues around the licensing.

There are plenty of options that are viable.

