Hi folks,

This week we will just have a worksession, so come and say hi, stay as long as you like (between 10-12), and work/code/etc.

Last week, Rich Pauloo gave a tutorial on using RMarkdown. All materials are up on the website <http://d-rug.github.io/blog/2017/Rich-Pauloo-on-using-RMarkdown> now. We screencast the event, so if you want to rewatch, see the video HERE <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CHBOVuo6RCo>.

Upcoming Presentations:
Nov 16: Kate Tiedman:  using raster /raster calculations in R
Nov 30: Ryan Peek: mapmaking with R/RStudio

PACKAGE OF THE WEEK:

Currently there are 11, 770 total packages on CRAN <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/>.

A few packages this week, in both tidyverse and base R worlds.

readxl <http://readxl.tidyverse.org/>: great for reading Excel based formats (both .xls and .xlsx) files
foreign <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/foreign/index.html>: reads all kinds of different data types, by 'Minitab', 'S', 'SAS', 'SPSS', 'Stata', 'Systat', 'Weka', 'dBase'
googlesheets <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/googlesheets/vignettes/basic-usage.html>: If you work in googledrive, this can be a really handy package. It plays well with/without pipes, and allows you to pull data directly from googlesheets. It's well written and documented as well. Double bonus.
Do you have a package you really enjoy using? Please send it/them my way! Here's a google form we can use to compile all of these: https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73.

If you want to see the packages that I've mentioned thus far this quarter, there's a table here <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vQH6BvP8p-YZOWpYFVIJYBa8AyscYgQB0Mone8NUKhlwKAA8UfGmUoIy22CO1AHOkNTR3Q4LSu2lvVm/pubhtml>.

Thanks much,
Adios,
Ryan

