I don't know anything about the package, but I suspect these errors
aren't directly related to the package.  It looks as if you are
somehow dealing with a matrix of numbers where (at least) one  column
is the same as, or nearly the same as, another.  Hence, the matrix is
singular, i.e., does not have an inverse.  Have a look at:

https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/76488/error-system-is-computationally-singular-when-running-a-glm

for instance.

