Hi D-RUGGies,

Tomorrow we'll have a presentation from Kate Tiedeman on using the raster package in R. There's some great expertise and info that can be shared for those that work on spatial data (vector or raster), so we are hoping to get some material out to you all.

We'll be screencasting the event, so if you want to chat or watch live (or later), see the video on youtube HERE <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mHz4wxo-Q4U>.

I'll post up materials/code after the presentation tomorrow.

And in a few weeks, I'll talk about mapmaking with RStudio (Nov 30th), which will focus a bit more on point data and vector data.

PACKAGE OF THE WEEK:

Currently there are 11, 840 total packages on CRAN <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/>.

A glut of packages this week that are all helpful or dependent on one another for working with spatial data. If you haven't already installed the rgdal package, you'll need it for most of the spatial packages. This isn't a complete list, but the main packages I think everyone should be aware of (please add to the google form <https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73> for others I'm missing):
sf
rgdal
sp
raster
ggmap
rgeos
maptools
maps
If you want to see the packages that I've mentioned thus far this quarter, there's a table here <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-1vQH6BvP8p-YZOWpYFVIJYBa8AyscYgQB0Mone8NUKhlwKAA8UfGmUoIy22CO1AHOkNTR3Q4LSu2lvVm/pubhtml>.

Hope to see you all tomorrow at 10am in the Library (DSI 360).

Thanks,
